  "question": {
    "text": "A thin circular ring of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is rotating about its axis with an angular speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Two particles having mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> each are now attached at diametrically opposite points. The angular speed of the ring will become:"
